# Global gitignore, referenced by core.excludesfile.
#
# These belong to the machine, not to any repository, so they are excluded once
# here rather than repeated in every project's .gitignore.

.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

.idea/
.vscode/settings.local.json
*.swp
*.swo

.direnv/
.venv/
__pycache__/

# AI agent state, which lands in whatever repository you happen to be working in.
#
# This machine installs three coding agents (claude-code, codex and opencode via the dev
# profile), and each writes its own directory into the working tree. They hold local
# session state and settings, not project configuration, so they belong to the machine —
# which is what this file is for.
#
# A project that genuinely wants to COMMIT one of these, to share agent instructions with a
# team, negates it there: `!.claude/` in the project's own .gitignore, or `git add -f`.
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.opencode/

# Local secrets must never be staged by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# These also hide legitimate files: a public certificate, or a test fixture.
# That is the intended trade — a silent skip is better than a leaked key — but
# when a match really should be committed, use `git add -f <path>`.
*.pem
*.key
